  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nTemperatures will remain warm through Friday with the continued \nsouthwest flow into Montana and ridge over the northern plains. \nHighs may reach the upper 90s in the southeast on Friday which \nlend to elevated Fire Weather concerns if wind gust can ramp up as\nwell. \n\nEarly next week as the upper ridge tilts westward and the west\ncoast trough closes off, another round of showers and\nthunderstorms is expected across the region. This is the second\nday for a strong precipitation total signal from Sunday night into\nMonday night. While these totals could still reduce in further\nforecasts, currently up to 1 inch is being teased at some\nlocations over these two periods. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo significant deviations from NBM made.",
